nagisa-rs

The Rust implementation is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

This is a port of word-segmentation and POS inference from nagisa 0.2.11,
originally implemented in Python/Cython using DyNet by Taishi Ikeda
(taishi-i) and contributors:
https://github.com/taishi-i/nagisa
https://pypi.org/project/nagisa/0.2.11/
Copyright (c) 2018 taishi-i
The upstream MIT license is reproduced in licenses/nagisa-MIT.txt.
The original pretrained dictionary is bundled in data/nagisa_v001.dict.
All original f32 model parameters are bundled without quantization in the
nagisa-rs-model data crate. Both assets remain under the upstream MIT
license. Source and asset hashes are recorded in data/manifest.json.

Unicode normalization and casing tables were generated from CPython
3.12.14 (Unicode 15.0.0). The Unicode data license is reproduced in
licenses/Unicode-3.0.txt.

The candidate POS feature ordering follows CPython 3.12.14's small-integer
set insertion, resizing and deletion behavior (Objects/setobject.c).
CPython is maintained by the Python Software Foundation and contributors:
https://github.com/python/cpython/tree/v3.12.14
Its license is reproduced in licenses/Python-2.0.txt.
